FEX thunks: 32-bit Vulkan for i386 guests under a guest base (SteamARM, Darwin host)

A 32-bit guest lives at host = base + guest. Every guest pointer a 32-bit host
thunk follows (get_pointer, host_layout<T*>) gets the base added, and a host
pointer given back to the guest (to_guest) loses it. The base comes from the
lxrt runtime. 64-bit thunks are unchanged.

Host pointers outside the guest window (Vulkan's dispatchable handles are
MoltenVK objects far above 4 GiB) are aliased into the window by the Vulkan
shim (shim/map32.c, lxrt_handle_alias) and converted back on the way in.
Guest-stack arguments of host->guest callbacks are built at their host
address and handed over as guest addresses.

Coverage: upstream leaves ~500 functions out of the 32-bit thunks, among them
what DXVK and VKD3D-Proton need (vkCmdDrawIndexed, vkCmdCopyBuffer2,
vkQueueSubmit2, push descriptors...). They are enabled here, except families
MoltenVK does not implement and whose structures thunkgen cannot repack
(ray tracing, video, micromaps, descriptor buffers/heaps, vendor extensions,
device groups...). Arrays of structures are repacked element by element
(generated custom implementations; thunkgen repacks one element), including
the Vulkan 1.3 "*2" copy/blit/resolve/submit structures, specialization info
and the shader stage of compute pipelines; the pNext table gains the
extension structures of the pinned Vulkan headers, and an unknown one is left
out of the chain instead of aborting.

